   "type": "teach",
   "heading": "Angle facts to remember",
   "html": "<p>Angles that meet <b>on a straight line</b> add up to <b>180°</b>. Angles <b>in a triangle</b> also add up to <b>180°</b>. Angles <b>around a point</b> make <b>360°</b>.</p><div class='figure'><svg viewBox=\"0 0 300 210\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polygon points=\"40,170 260,170 150,40\" fill=\"#6C8FF622\" stroke=\"#2A2E45\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"56\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#3D6FF0\">60°</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#3D6FF0\">70°</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#E4572E\">?</text></svg></div><div class='example-box'>Third angle = 180 − 60 − 70 = <b>50°</b> ✅</div>"
  },
  {
   "type": "teach",
